    <main>
        <section>
            <p>Wellness Hills Mental Health Treatment provides outpatient mental health care for adults in Chester, New Jersey. Services include individual and group therapy, psychiatry, medication management, Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP), and Partial Hospitalization Program (PHP).</p>
            <p>This resource guide brings together information about the Wellness Hills treatment environment, available services, the admissions process, and resources for families exploring mental health treatment in New Jersey.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Inside Wellness Hills</h2>
            <p>A recent News12 segment featured Wellness Hills Mental Health Treatment in Chester and Program Director Leigh Rasmussen, LPC, LCADC.</p>
            <p>The segment explored several aspects of mental health care, including recognizing changes in mental well-being, creating a welcoming treatment environment, and making access to care more responsive when someone decides to seek help.</p>
            <p>Leigh Rasmussen described the Wellness Hills setting as welcoming and intimate, with an emphasis on helping people feel comfortable when they enter treatment.</p>
            <div class="card">
                <strong>Watch the Segment:</strong> 
                <a href="https://newjersey.news12.com/2026/08/31/managing-mental-health/3ZUzZcdp2KpZ7gDNM46FgL" target="_blank" rel="noopener">News12: Managing Mental Health</a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Meet Leigh Rasmussen, LPC, LCADC</h2>
            <p>Leigh Rasmussen is the Program Director at Wellness Hills Mental Health Treatment.</p>
            <p>She is a Licensed Professional Counselor and Licensed Clinical Alcohol and Drug Counselor. Leigh earned a B.A. in Psychology from Rutgers University and a Master's degree in Mental Health Counseling from Capella University, graduating Summa Cum Laude in 2018 while working full-time.</p>
            <p>Her professional background includes direct care, management, and clinical support. She joined Rolling Hills in 2025 to help launch Wellness Hills.</p>
            <p><a href="https://wellnesshillsmentalhealth.com/staff/leigh-rasmussen-lpc-lcadc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn more about Leigh Rasmussen</a></p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Mental Health Treatment in New Jersey</h2>
            <p>Wellness Hills in Chester provides outpatient mental health care for adults. Treatment options may include different levels of structure depending on individual needs and clinical appropriateness.</p>

            <h3>Depression Treatment</h3>
            <p>Adults experiencing depression can explore outpatient treatment that may include therapy, psychiatry, and medication management.</p>
            <p><a href="https://wellnesshillsmentalhealth.com/conditions/depression/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn more about depression treatment in New Jersey</a></p>

            <h3>Anxiety Treatment</h3>
            <p>Anxiety-related concerns can be addressed through outpatient mental health services and structured programming when appropriate.</p>
            <p><a href="https://wellnesshillsmentalhealth.com/conditions/anxiety/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn more about anxiety treatment in New Jersey</a></p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>From First Call to Ongoing Care</h2>
            <p>The treatment pathway can begin with a conversation about what is happening and what type of support may be appropriate.</p>

            <div class="flowchart">
                <div class="flow-step">First Call</div>
                <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="flow-step">Assessment</div>
                <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="flow-step">Appropriate Level of Care</div>
                <div class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</div>
                <div class="flow-step">Ongoing Support</div>
            </div>

            <p>Available outpatient levels may include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Outpatient mental health treatment</li>
                <li>Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP)</li>
                <li>Partial Hospitalization Program (PHP)</li>
            </ul>
            <p><em>The appropriate level of care depends on individual needs and clinical appropriateness.</em></p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Starting the Admissions Process</h2>
            <p>The Wellness Hills call center is available 24 hours a day, seven days a week.</p>
            <p>The admissions process can help individuals and families:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Explain what is happening</li>
                <li>Discuss potential treatment needs</li>
                <li>Review insurance information</li>
                <li>Complete the appropriate pre-screen and assessment process</li>
                <li>Determine whether available services are an appropriate fit</li>
            </ul>
            <p>When an individual is an appropriate fit, admission may be available within 24 hours. Timing depends on clinical appropriateness and available services.</p>
        </section>

